#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
PowerShell Script Redactor
==========================

Single-file GUI tool. Load or paste a PowerShell script in the top box; the
bottom box shows a redacted copy, updated automatically, with every redaction
highlighted in red.

 - VS Code "Dark+" PowerShell syntax highlighting in both boxes
 - ~30 detectors: secrets and API keys, GUIDs labelled from context as tenant /
   app / subscription IDs, emails, SIDs, LDAP DNs, UNC paths, SharePoint and
   onmicrosoft domains, IPs, MACs, internal hostnames. Each one toggleable.
 - Usernames are found by context (account-looking variables such as
   $targetUser, and account parameters such as -SamAccountName), then that same
   value is redacted everywhere else it appears in the script
 - Custom company names, terms and regex patterns; an allow list for public
   endpoints that should survive, such as graph.microsoft.com
 - Placeholders are numbered only when a label has more than one distinct value,
   and the same value always gets the same number
 - Arrows next to the count jump through the redactions (also F3 / Shift-F3)
 - Copy or export the result; settings are written back into THIS file, so it
   stays a single portable file (falls back to a sidecar .json if the file is
   read-only or the script has been frozen with PyInstaller)

Run:  python ps_redactor.py      (requires Python 3.8+ with tkinter)
"""

